menu "Firefly Valve Node"

    config FIREFLY_VALVE_TEST_MODE
        bool "Run bench self-test sequence on boot"
        default y
        help
            Runs the DRAINMASTER-VALVES.md bring-up order steps 1-3 on
            every boot: clicks each of the 8 relays individually, attempts
            a deliberately unsafe mask and confirms the interlock refuses
            it, then proves the independent watchdog releases the relays
            even when the driving code doesn't call release itself.

            Safe with no valve or sense wiring connected — everything here
            is a relay click and an I2C readback. Turn this off once
            bring-up is done and real ESP-NOW-driven valve control lands
            (a later issue), so a production boot doesn't click every
            relay before going idle.

endmenu
